description:
Toast is driven by building a platform that helps our customers adapt, take control, and get back to what they do best: building the businesses they love. International expansion is a critical growth engine for Toast's future.&nbsp;

Outside the US, we currently operate in Canada, UK, Ireland, and Australia and are actively growing our share in these markets. As we move into the next phase of growth, the complexity of our platform surface area and customer segments is increasing materially. We are looking for a commercially-minded (Senior) Director of Product Management to enable this growth.

As a (Senior) Director of Product, International, you will lead the team of product managers to own the vision, strategy, and roadmap around upmarket expansion to support larger (15+ locations) groups, accelerating integration partner availability to ensure customers can use Toast alongside their preferred tech stack, and&nbsp; expansion of our FinTech / payments pricing capabilities. Scaling and managing these domains require someone who can work credibly with customers, GTM teams, engineers, executive stakeholders, and external partners in equal measure.&nbsp;

This is a London based-role, partnering closely with teams across Canada, Australia, U.S., Ireland, and India, and a key part of our EMEA leadership team. This is a rare opportunity to shape the future of how Toast serves customers in new markets.

A day in the life (Responsibilities)&nbsp;

• Drive Strategy and Execution: Set the strategic direction across upmarket, partner, and payment expansion with a focus on how those areas interact and reinforce each other to meet the north star goals for the International line of business. Partner with engineering and product teams across Toast's platform teams to ship international features in their area. Navigate competing roadmaps, set clear success criteria, and hold delivery against contractual commitments.

• Voice of Customer: Engage directly with customers, partners, and GTM teams to understand real needs - and use that grounding to pressure-test roadmap priorities and push back on assumptions that don't hold up in the field. Represent the voice of international customers as the PM voice for our global restaurant and hospitality brands in roadmap discussions, cross-functional reviews, and executive conversations.&nbsp;

• Lead Through Influence: Champion cross-functional delivery across Product, Engineering, Design, Legal/Compliance, Hardware, Commerce, Risk, Finance, and Operations. This role has direct exposure to C-suite leadership and regular involvement in executive-level roadmap and strategy discussions.&nbsp;

• Develop a World-Class Team and OS: Hire, coach, and develop a world-class team of Product Managers across multiple regions. Scale our operating model grounded in ownership, accountability, clarity, and exceptional execution.&nbsp;

• Embrace and advocate for the use of AI tools to accelerate product discovery, streamline execution, and explore new product experiences - helping shape how we build and what we build.

What you'll need to thrive (Requirements)

• 15+ years of product management experience in SaaS or FinTech, with at least 5 years in a senior leadership role. You've owned a portfolio of products for a market, not just a feature area.

• Commercial instincts. You understand how product decisions translate into revenue, retention, and customer value, and you make prioritization decisions accordingly.

• Comfort with ambiguity at the charter level - you have shaped product direction from scratch, not just executed against someone else's vision.

• A track record of working across a complex stakeholder map - engineering, GTM, finance, external partners - that do not report to you. You are comfortable driving alignment without losing sharpness in the process.

• Strong people leadership. You build teams, give direct feedback, develop careers, and hold a high bar for product thinking without micromanaging exec

About the Company &nbsp;

At Torc, we have always believed that autonomous vehicle technology will transform how we travel, move freight, and do business. &nbsp;
A leader in autonomous driving since 2007, Torc has spent over a decade commercializing our solutions with experienced partners.  Now a part of the Daimler family , we are focused solely on developing software for automated trucks to transform how the world moves freight. &nbsp;
Join us and catapult your career with the company that helped pioneer autonomous technology, and the first AV software company with the vision to partner directly with a truck manufacturer. &nbsp;

Meet the Team &nbsp;

The Senior Autonomy Core Frameworks Software Engineer plays a critical role in architecting and advancing the foundational frameworks that underpin Torc's autonomous driving stack. This role helps in owning technical direction for the software in core autonomy components, helping to raise the bar on code quality, and driving improvements across the autonomy software. &nbsp;

As a senior technical leader, you will collaborate closely with the Behavior and Perception teams within Autonomy to design robust, composable architectural patterns that serve as the foundation for safe, performant, reliable autonomous operation. This position demands deep technical expertise in software architecture and autonomous vehicle fundamentals. &nbsp;

What You’ll Do &nbsp;

• Lead the architecture, design, implementation, and evolution of core frameworks that serve as the foundation for Torc's autonomous driving stack, including state management, inter- component communication, abstraction layers, and common utilities used across all software systems.

• Drive&nbsp; the technical direction for real-time C++ architectural components and patterns responsible for reliable system-wide data flow, component coordination, error handling, and operational observability.

• Establish scalable architectural patterns and abstractions that enable autonomous driving capabilities while driving technical tradeoff discussions and long-term design decisions that shape the entire platform.

• Collaborate across Behavior and Perception teams to keep integration boundaries clean and shared abstractions coherent.

• Lead architecture reviews, design discussions, and code reviews while&nbsp; establishing engineering standards that improve reliability, maintainability, testability, and scalability across the platform.

• Mentor software engineers through technical coaching, architectural guidance, and day-to-day collaboration while raising engineering standards and fostering technical excellence across the organization.

• Champion architectural quality through systematic validation, comprehensive testing strategies, observability frameworks, and production readiness practices that ensure platform robustness at scale.

• Contribute to&nbsp; root cause analysis of complex platform-level issues and drive architectural improvements that enhance system reliability, performance, and operational resilience.

• Define and evolve simulation and validation frameworks that enable rigorous testing of core architectural components across diverse operational scenarios and edge cases.

• Evaluate emerging architectural patterns,&nbsp; systems research, and advanced techniques that can strengthen the platform's foundation and enable future autonomous driving capabilities.

• Communicate complex architectural concepts and technical vision effectively across engineering teams, product, and leadership while building consensus around platf orm direction and technical strategy. &nbsp;

What You’ll Need to Succeed &nbsp;

• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Robotics, Electrical Engineering, or related technical discipline with 8+ years of professional software engineering experience, or

• Master's degree with 6+ years of professional experience, or

